    "relatedAirdropId": "sonic",
    "content": "Sonic Labs, the architectural evolution of the Fantom blockchain, has unveiled the operational roadmap for its eagerly anticipated mainnet launch. Engineered to deliver over 10,000 transactions per second (TPS) with true sub-second finality (approximately 700 milliseconds), Sonic represents one of the most substantial performance leaps in Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM) history.\n\n## Technical Architecture and the Carmen Storage Engine\n\nAt the core of Sonic's performance breakthrough is a complete redesign of the state management layer. Rather than relying on traditional EVM storage primitives such as LevelDB or PebbleDB, Sonic introduces **Carmen**, a proprietary custom flat database engine:\n\n- **State Access Latency Reduction**: Carmen reduces disk input/output operations by up to 90%, allowing smart contracts to read and write state variables without thread contention.\n- **Optimized Sonic Virtual Machine (SVM)**: The execution environment compiles smart contract bytecode into optimized native machine instructions, enabling sustained high-throughput throughput during peak network demand.\n- **1:1 Token Migration Gateway**: Existing Fantom ($FTM) holders can seamlessly migrate their holdings 1:1 to the native Sonic ($S) token through a two-way canonical bridge.\n\n> \"Sonic is not merely an incremental speed improvement; it fundamentally resolves the persistent storage bottlenecks that have constrained EVM rollups and alt-L1s for years,\" stated the Sonic engineering council in their technical specification.\n\n## The 200 Million $S Airdrop and Fee Monetization\n\nTo cultivate a robust ecosystem from genesis, the Sonic Foundation has allocated approximately 200 million $S tokens specifically for early community contributors, testnet users, and liquidity providers. \n\nThe incentive mechanism integrates **Fee Monetization (FeeM)**, a protocol-level revenue model where developers receive up to 90% of the gas fees generated by their smart contracts. This model aligns developer economic incentives directly with user volume and network utility.\n\n## Key Actions for Airdrop Participants\n\n- **Testnet Interaction**: Bridge testnet assets via the official Sonic testnet portal and execute regular swaps on native DEX protocols.\n- **Validator Node Staking**: Deploy community nodes on the public testnet to establish on-chain telemetry and hardware uptime records.\n- **Arcade Engagement**: Participate in the Sonic Arcade mini-games to stress-test high-frequency microtransaction throughput."
